1. Definitions

"Licensor" means Yannick Triqueneaux.

"You" means the individual or legal entity exercising rights under this
License.

"Licensed Work" means the original source code, scripts, templates,
documentation, and other copyrightable material distributed in this
repository by the Licensor. It excludes Third-Party Components.

"Core Work" means every part of the Licensed Work located outside the `Games/`
directory, including Engine, AssistantHost, GameHost, Launcher, build-system
files, development scripts, infrastructure, and related documentation.

"Core Modification" means any change, adaptation, translation, extension,
fork, or derivative work of the Core Work.

"Game Content" means source code, build files, scripts, designs, assets, and
other material located inside a Game Project's `Games/<game-name>/` directory.
Game Content is not a Core Modification, even when it was copied or adapted
from `Games/BaseGame/`.

"Game Project" means a game or interactive software project created, generated,
compiled, linked, or developed using any material part of the Licensed Work,
including its Engine, Launcher, AssistantHost, GameHost, build scripts,
BaseGame, or code-generation and assistant workflow.

"Core Modification Source" means the preferred form for modifying a Core
Modification, including its source code, build files, scripts, and supporting
material reasonably necessary to build and understand it. Core Modification
Source expressly excludes all Game Content.

"Commercial Game" means a Game Project for which access to a copy is provided
to a player in exchange for money or other valuable consideration.

"Sold Copy" means each paid copy, license, activation, key, download
entitlement, or other paid grant of access to a Commercial Game provided to a
player. A copy fully refunded or charged back may be excluded or credited in
the reporting period in which the refund or chargeback occurs. Free copies
provided for no consideration are not Sold Copies.

"Third-Party Components" means software, content, or other material identified
as originating from third parties, including raylib, Dear ImGui, rlImGui, and
nlohmann/json. Those components remain governed exclusively by their respective
licenses.

