3. Mandatory Sharing of Core Modifications

You must provide the Licensor with complete Core Modification Source for every
Core Modification, including Core Modifications kept private or used only
internally.
The first delivery must occur no later than the earliest of:

a. 30 days after the Core Modification is distributed, published, sold, or
   otherwise made available to another person;
b. 30 days after the Core Modification is first used commercially; or
c. 90 days after the Core Modification is first created.

After the first delivery, You must provide updated Core Modification Source at
least once per calendar quarter while development continues.

Delivery must be made to mmotoobusy@gmail.com or through another
submission method designated in writing by the Licensor. The delivery must be
reasonably complete, readable, and sufficient to build and understand the
Core Modification using ordinarily available development tools.

Sharing with the Licensor does not, by itself, require public disclosure.

For clarity, You are never required to disclose or deliver Game Content,
including gameplay code, game-specific systems, designs, art, audio, narrative
content, or other files inside `Games/<game-name>/`.

